From: OpenVMMS Maintainers <fastdesk@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH 1/1] mesh_rpc: cancel pending RPCs and drop responses on client disconnect
Upstream-Base: microsoft/openvmm@c4419be15ab702194f0a25c294bd2f6187804824

In `mesh_rpc::Server::serve_connection`, closing the ttrpc client socket
previously did not cancel the connection's `CancelContext`, and `send_task`
attempted to write responses back to the closed stream.

This patch wires `CancelContext::new().with_cancel()` and a `peer_closed`
flag into `serve_connection`: when `read_message` reaches EOF or errors,
`cancel.cancel()` cancels all pending RPCs on that connection and `send_task`
drops their responses rather than writing to the dead socket.

Behavioral impact across every ttrpc service:
- Any ttrpc client that closes its socket before receiving a response now
  cancels all pending RPCs on that connection (via `CancelContext`) and their
  responses are dropped.

Rationale in this repository:
- OpenVMM's `VmService::WaitVm` stores a single `(CancelContext, response)`
  waiter per VM. Cancelling `WaitVm`'s `CancelContext` when `openvmmsd` closes
  the socket during `daemon stop` / `SIGTERM` lets a restarted daemon cleanly
  re-adopt the running VM and re-attach `WaitVm` without hitting
  `"wait VM already in flight"`.

Carry forward or upstream when syncing `openvmm/` past `c4419be15ab702194f0a25c294bd2f6187804824`.
